- Added an hourly cleanup that deletes Windows MDM command history (raw device responses, command results, and the commands themselves) once it has gone 30 days without being recorded or updated, so those tables no longer grow without bound. Commands still waiting to run, and the wipe command a host's wiped status depends on, are kept regardless of age. The retention window is configurable with `mdm.windows_command_retention` (`FLEET_MDM_WINDOWS_COMMAND_RETENTION`); setting it to 0 disables the cleanup.
